# Rank 1343 / CVE-2022-23514: Loofah's HTML5 attribute scrubber stripped absolute
# `url(...)` references out of the SVG attributes that may carry a local reference
# with an unanchored regular expression substitution, and the substitution's cost
# is quadratic in the length of the attacker-supplied attribute value (CWE-1333
# inefficient regular expression complexity, CWE-400).
#
# `Scrub.scrub_attributes` (lib/loofah/html5/scrub.rb:54-56) reaches, for every
# attribute named in `SafeList::SVG_ATTR_VAL_ALLOWS_REF` (`fill`, `stroke`,
# `filter`, `clip-path` and the rest),
# `attr_node.value = attr_node.value.gsub(/url\s*\(\s*[^#\s][^)]+?\)/m, " ")`.
# The pattern is unanchored and applied globally, so `gsub` retries it at every
# `url(` in the value, and each retry grows `[^)]+?` one character at a time to
# the end of the value when no `)` follows -- an attribute value built out of
# repeated `url(` prefixes with no closing parenthesis costs O(n^2). The
# attribute value is markup the caller handed the sanitizer, which is the input
# a sanitizer exists to accept, so the bound is entirely the attacker's.
#
# The fixing commit a6e0a1ab90675a17b1b2be189129d94139e4b143 touches lib/loofah/html5/scrub.rb plus the two
# test fixtures that recorded the old output, replaces the `gsub` call with
# `scrub_attribute_that_allows_local_ref(attr_node)`, and implements that method
# with `Crass::Parser.new(attr_node.value).parse_component_values`, keeping the
# `:url` component values whose target starts with `#` along with `:hash`,
# `:ident` and `:string` values and dropping everything else
# is needed.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap, and two separate absences block it.
#
# First, the pattern is not classified as backtracking-prone, and that
# classification is correct as far as it goes: `regexambig.Ambiguous` answers
# false for `url\s*\(\s*[^#\s][^)]+?\)` because the pattern has no overlapping
# quantified branches at all. `\s*` is followed by `\(` and by `[^#\s]`, both
# disjoint from `\s`, and `[^)]+?` is followed by `\)`, which it excludes. Its
# cost is polynomial in the number of start positions, not exponential in one
# match attempt, and polynomial backtracking is a class the engine does not
# model. So `rubyRegexMayBacktrack`
# (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/ruby.go:1130) leaves the literal a plain
# `nir.Const` instead of the `__regex.match` call it synthesises for a
# backtracking-prone literal, and no `code.RegexMatch`, `code.RegexMatchSink` or
# `code.CatastrophicRegex` label is ever emitted. `vyql match` over a repro of
# the vulnerable branch reports no source and no sink whatsoever; the single
# label is `threat.CharFilter` on `attr_node.value.gsub`. A bounded scan of the
# real checkout at the vulnerable revision (`--cache off --max-ram 6GB`, 219
# findings, 217 at or above high) reports nothing in lib/loofah/html5/scrub.rb --
# 216 of those 219 are VYQL-SEC-025 on a bundled `benchmark/www.slashdot.com.html`
# fixture.
#
# Second, there is no source side either. `vyql resolve` over the repro reports
# `node.attribute_nodes.each` unresolved, and `vyql/bindings/ruby/` carries no
# Nokogiri binding at all, so nothing labels a parsed attribute's value as
# untrusted markup. VYQL-DOS-002 asks for `core.UserControlledData` to reach
# `code.RegexMatchSink`, and the source half is missing independently of the sink
# half. Only the presence rule VYQL-DOS-003 (`issue code.CatastrophicRegex`)
# could fire on the label alone, and a probe binding emitting that concept
# confirms it does -- but a `presenceNode` binding cannot address a regex
# literal: the probe's four findings land on the enclosing module and class scope
# nodes at scrub.rb:1, 2, 3 and 5, not on the pattern. The label has to come from
# the frontend, which is why this is not a binding.
#
# Extending the classification is what a fix would mean, and it does not survive
# its own precision measurement. Over the `lib/` trees of loofah, rack and
# sanitize -- 268 Ruby regex literals, all three libraries whose job is handling
# untrusted input -- a label for "quantified negated character class" flags 7,
# exactly one of them this vulnerability; the other six are ordinary and safe
# (`/bytes=([^;]+)/`, `/\A\/[^#]*\z/`, `/[^;]*/`, `/\A[^\/:]+:\d+\z/`,
# `/\A(["'])?[^"']+\1\z/`, and sanitize's scheme extractor). The narrower shape
# "negated class quantifier immediately followed by the literal it excludes"
# flags 2, the second being rack's anchored `/\A[^\/:]+:\d+\z/` -- and that idiom
# is the recommended way to write a delimited scan, so it cannot be a soundness
# criterion. The broadest shape, "unanchored open-ended quantifier", flags 11,
# `/\s+/` among them. One true positive in seven to eleven, on libraries this
# small, is worse than no label.
#
# The reason no pattern-shape criterion works here is visible in that sample:
# rack's `/bytes=([^;]+)/`, matched against the untrusted `Range` request header,
# is structurally the same regex as loofah's -- fixed literal prefix, quantified
# negated character class, unanchored -- and it is fine. What separates them is
# not readable off the pattern. It is that loofah's operand is an unbounded
# attacker-supplied SVG attribute value, and what the fixed revision changes is the
# algorithm that reads it, from a regex substitution to CSS component-value
# parsing, not any structural property of the pattern.
#
# The isolating pair below places the boundary with no Loofah or Nokogiri API:
# the same `case`/`when` shape over a method parameter reports VYQL-DOS-002 when
# the pattern carries a nested ambiguous quantifier, and reports nothing when it
# carries this CVE's pattern instead. The two differ only in the quantifier
# structure of the literal. The gap is the cost model: `regexambig.Ambiguous` is
# the one shared answer for three call sites -- ruby.go:1135,
# javascript.go:1113 and lowering.go:2157, the last covering every language
# without its own frontend check -- so teaching it polynomial backtracking is a
# new classification with solver-wide effect on what gets labelled, not a
# localized correction to a construct it handles. Deciding which
# polynomial shapes are reportable is design work, and the measurement above says
# the obvious candidates are not. No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1343: the SVG local-ref attribute scrubber substitutes with a quadratic regex"
  lang ruby
  file lib/loofah/html5/scrub.rb
  profile library
  reject VYQL-DOS-001
  reject VYQL-DOS-002
  reject VYQL-DOS-003
  code
  ```
  require "cgi"
  require "crass"

  module Loofah
    module HTML5
      module Scrub
        DATA_ATTRIBUTE_NAME = /\Adata-[\w-]+\z/

        class << self
          def scrub_attributes(node)
            node.attribute_nodes.each do |attr_node|
              attr_name = if attr_node.namespace
                "#{attr_node.namespace.prefix}:#{attr_node.node_name}"
              else
                attr_node.node_name
              end

              if attr_name =~ DATA_ATTRIBUTE_NAME
                next
              end

              unless SafeList::ALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES.include?(attr_name)
                attr_node.remove
                next
              end

              if SafeList::SVG_ATTR_VAL_ALLOWS_REF.include?(attr_name)
                attr_node.value = attr_node.value.gsub(/url\s*\(\s*[^#\s][^)]+?\)/m, " ") if attr_node.value
              end

              if SafeList::SVG_ALLOW_LOCAL_HREF.include?(node.name) && attr_name == "xlink:href" && attr_node.value =~ /^\s*[^#\s].*/m
                attr_node.remove
                next
              end
            end
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1343: the local-ref scrubber reading component values with the CSS parser is clean"
  lang ruby
  file lib/loofah/html5/scrub.rb
  profile library
  reject VYQL-DOS-001
  reject VYQL-DOS-002
  reject VYQL-DOS-003
  code
  ```
  require "cgi"
  require "crass"

  module Loofah
    module HTML5
      module Scrub
        DATA_ATTRIBUTE_NAME = /\Adata-[\w-]+\z/

        class << self
          def scrub_attributes(node)
            node.attribute_nodes.each do |attr_node|
              attr_name = if attr_node.namespace
                "#{attr_node.namespace.prefix}:#{attr_node.node_name}"
              else
                attr_node.node_name
              end

              if attr_name =~ DATA_ATTRIBUTE_NAME
                next
              end

              unless SafeList::ALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES.include?(attr_name)
                attr_node.remove
                next
              end

              if SafeList::SVG_ATTR_VAL_ALLOWS_REF.include?(attr_name)
                scrub_attribute_that_allows_local_ref(attr_node)
              end

              if SafeList::SVG_ALLOW_LOCAL_HREF.include?(node.name) && attr_name == "xlink:href" && attr_node.value =~ /^\s*[^#\s].*/m
                attr_node.remove
                next
              end
            end
          end

          def scrub_attribute_that_allows_local_ref(attr_node)
            return unless attr_node.value

            nodes = Crass::Parser.new(attr_node.value).parse_component_values

            values = nodes.map do |node|
              case node[:node]
              when :url
                if node[:value].start_with?("#")
                  node[:raw]
                else
                  nil
                end
              when :hash, :ident, :string
                node[:raw]
              else
                nil
              end
            end.compact

            attr_node.value = values.join(" ")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

# The isolating pair. Same shape, same operand, no library API: only the
# quantifier structure of the literal differs.

test "rank1343 pair: a nested ambiguous quantifier in the url() pattern is reported"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  expect VYQL-DOS-002
  code
  ```
  class LocalRefScrubber
    def call(value)
      case value
      when /url\s*\(\s*([^#\s]+)+\)/m
        ""
      else
        value
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1343 pair: the quadratic url() pattern in the same shape is not reported"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  reject VYQL-DOS-002
  code
  ```
  class LocalRefScrubber
    def call(value)
      case value
      when /url\s*\(\s*[^#\s][^)]+?\)/m
        ""
      else
        value
      end
    end
  end
  ```
